istent answer using majority voting.\")\nprint(sa)\nr = read_pdf(start_page=19, end_page=22)\nprint([p['page'] for p in r.get('pages', [])])\n```", "code_action": "sa = save_answer(section=\"reasoning\", question_id=\"self_consistency_selection\", answer={\"value\": \"majority voting\"}, evidence_id=\"ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3\", page=10, quote=\"Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.\")\nprint(sa)\nr = read_pdf(start_page=19, end_page=22)\nprint([p['page'] for p in r.get('pages', [])])", "observations": "Execution logs:\n{'section': 'reasoning', 'question_id': 'self_consistency_selection', 'saved': True}\n[19, 20, 21, 22]\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone", "observations_images": null, "action_output": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 7222, "output_tokens": 508, "total_tokens": 7730}, "is_final_answer": false}}
