 et al. split planner, caller and summarizer across different LLMs. Tool selection and result summarization remain difficult skills.\", ['ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62','ev-7f4d5e2fe0886c80c09b','ev-e5b9499e130a976eefe2'], 'tool_use')\nr5 = read_pdf(start_page=41, end_page=52)\nfor p in r5['pages']:\n    PDF[p['page']] = p['text']\nprint(r_a, r_b, n)\nprint(sorted(PDF), {k: len(v) for k, v in PDF.items()})\n```", "reasoning_content": "We have Toolformer tools, ToolBench API count 16,464. Need to save tool_use answers once evidence delivered. Page 23 is delivered (ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62). Let's save tool_use answers now with quote from page 23.\n\nQuote: \"A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar. Further works extend this to a larger range of tools. ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI, a large dataset of publicly available REST APIs.\"\n\nNeed toolformer_tools with abbreviated format: calculator, question_answering, search_engine, translation_system? \"使用 calculator、question_answering 这样的简写格式\" - so \"translation\", \"calendar\", \"search\"? Hmm. The abbreviations: calculator, question_answering, search_engine? Actually \"question-answering system\" -> question_answering. \"search engine\" -> search_engine? Or \"search\"? \"translation system\" -> translation. \"calendar\" -> calendar. I'd use [\"calculator\",\"question_answering\",\"search_engine\",\"translation\",\"calendar\"].\n\nLet's save answer and also write a note for tool_use (based on pages 20-23 delivered). Also need to continue reading pages 41-52.\n\nBudget: requests after response 27, fine.\n\nLet's do: save_answer tool_use both, write_note tool_use, read_pdf 41-52.\n\nBut careful: each action one block; save_answer and read_pdf independent? Save answers require evidence_id from delivered evidence — page 23 evidence id ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62. Yes.\n\nBut \"only ONE fenced Python block\" — can inc