tor": "page:49", "required": true, "page": 49, "valid": true, "atomic": true, "chars": 4295, "exposed": true}, {"id": "ev-42cada09d7411017eb46", "source": "paper.pdf", "version": "b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c", "locator": "page:50", "required": true, "page": 50, "valid": true, "atomic": true, "chars": 4663, "exposed": true}, {"id": "ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9", "source": "paper.pdf", "version": "b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c", "locator": "page:51", "required": true, "page": 51, "valid": true, "atomic": true, "chars": 3844, "exposed": true}, {"id": "ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3", "source": "paper.pdf", "version": "b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c", "locator": "page:52", "required": true, "page": 52, "valid": true, "atomic": true, "chars": 4072, "exposed": true}], "notes": {"overview": {"id": "overview", "content": "Pages 1-3: Paper defines agentic LLMs as LLMs that (1) reason, (2) act, (3) interact; literature is organized according to these three categories. Contributions list adds details: category 1 = reasoning, reflection, retrieval to improve decision making; category 2 = tools and robot integration producing assistants in medicine/finance; category 3 = interaction, multi-agent simulations, role-playing, open-ended agent societies, emergent behavior. Figure 1 gives a virtuous cycle: retrieval enables tool use, reflection improves multi-agent collaboration, reasoning benefits all; feedback loops generate new training data. A research agenda is in Section 5, Table 4. Still to read: Section 1.2 Literature Selection (p.5) for search methods, Section 2 (reasoning, p.8-19), Section 3 (acting, p.20-30), Section 4 (interacting, p.31-47), Section 5 (p.48-52).", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "evidence_ids": ["ev-03c9580cc4ea3469a3d3", "ev-84af1a450301aa5252ba", "ev-c3c928f38ebc0ac0c6cd"], "valid": true, "request": 3}, "tool_use": {"id": "tool_use", "content": "Tool use (pages 20-23): agents act through APIs, robotic planning and vision-language-action models. Toolformer self-trains to decide which API to call, when, which arguments, and how to use results; it tests a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar. ToolBench contains 16,464 RapidAPI APIs; ToolAlpaca covers 400 APIs and 3938 instances; Gorilla adds APIBench. Shen et al. split planner, caller and summarizer across different LLMs. Tool selection and result summarization remain difficult skills.", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "evidence_ids": ["ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62", "ev-7f4d5e2fe0886c80c09b", "ev-e5b9499e130a976eefe2"], "valid": true, "request": 13}}, "answers": {"reasoning": {"self_consistency_selection": {"answer": "majority voting", "evidence_id": "ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3", "page": 10, "quote": "Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting."}, "tot_search": {"answer": ["breadth_first", "depth_first"], "evidence_id": "ev-4049593a30e2846f8394", "page": 13, "quote": "The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller."}}, "tool_use": {"toolformer_tools": {"answer": ["calculator", "question_answering", "search_engine", "translation", "calendar"], "evidence_id": "ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62", "page": 23, "quote": "A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar."}, "toolbench_api_count": {"answer": 16464, "evidence_id": "ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62", "page": 23, "quote": "ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI, a large dataset of publicly available REST APIs."}}}, "section_text": {}}}
