'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:45', 'required': True, 'page': 45, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4456, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-75546d247dedb90561b5', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:46', 'required': True, 'page': 46, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4646, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:47', 'required': True, 'page': 47, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 5018, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-aa9b9dbdfec8c640b495', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:48', 'required': True, 'page': 48, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4375, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-6e64db9ec6bfa8f9417f', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:49', 'required': True, 'page': 49, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4295, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-42cada09d7411017eb46', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:50', 'required': True, 'page': 50, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4663, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:51', 'required': True, 'page': 51, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 3844, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:52', 'required': True, 'page': 52, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4072, 'exposed': True}], 'notes': {'overview': {'id': 'overview', 'content': 'Pages 1-3: Paper defines agentic LLMs as LLMs that (1) reason, (2) act, (3) interact; literature is organized according to these three categories. Contributions list adds details: category 1 = reasoning, reflection, retrieval to improve decision making; category 2 = tools and robot integration producing assistants in medicine/finance; category 3 = interaction, multi-agent simulations, role-playing, open-ended agent societies, emergent behavior. Figure 1 gives a virtuous cycle: retrieval enables tool use, reflection improves multi-agent collaboration, reasoning benefits all; feedback loops generate new training data. A research agenda is in Section 5, Table 4. Still to read: Section 1.2 Literature Selection (p.5) for search methods, Section 2 (reasoning, p.8-19), Section 3 (acting, p.20-30), Section 4 (interacting, p.31-47), Section 5 (p.48-52).', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-03c9580cc4ea3469a3d3', 'ev-84af1a450301aa5252ba', 'ev-c3c928f38ebc0ac0c6cd'], 'valid': True, 'request': 3}, 'tool_use': {'id': 'tool_use', 'content': 'Tool use (pages 20-23): agents act through APIs, robotic planning and vision-language-action models. Toolformer self-trains to decide which API to call, when, which arguments, and how to use results; it tests a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar. ToolBench contains 16,464 RapidAPI APIs; ToolAlpaca covers 400 APIs and 3938 instances; Gorilla adds APIBench. Shen et al. split planner, caller and summarizer across different LLMs. Tool selection and result summarization remain difficult skills.', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62', 'ev-7f4d5e2fe0886c80c09b', 'ev-e5b9499e130a976eefe2'], 'valid': True, 'request': 13}}, 'answers': {'reasoning': {'self_consistency_selection': {'answer': 'majority voting', 'evidence_id': 'ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3', 'page': 10, 'quote': 'Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.'}, 'tot_search': {'answer': ['breadth_first', 'depth_first'], 'evidence_id': 'ev-4049593a30e2846f8394', 'page': 13, 'quote': 'The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.'}}, 'tool_use': {'toolformer_tools': {'answer': ['calculator', 'question_answering', 'search_engine', 'translation', 'calendar'], 'evidence_id': 'ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62', 'page': 23, 'quote': 'A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar.'}, 'toolbench_api_count': {'answer': 16464, 'evidence_id': 'ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62', 'page': 23, 'quote': 'ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI, a large dataset of publicly available REST APIs.'}}}, 'section_text': {}}\n{'requested': [{'id': 'ev-03c9580cc4ea3469a3d3', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:1'}, {'id': 'ev-c3c928f38ebc0ac0c6cd', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:2'}, {'id': 'ev-84af1a450301aa5252ba', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:3'}, {'id': 'ev-dbca06e364385e22f3c5', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:5'}, {'id': 'ev-345e6706309ac04ee927', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:36'}, {'id': 'ev-98a30db9253fff6cc9da', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:37'}, {'id': 'ev-2f8846ab5b1bc7072a1b', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:38'}, {'id': 'ev-76027d4e758f97793930', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:39'}], 'queued': [{'id': 'ev-03c9580cc4ea3469a3d3', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:1'}, {'id': 'ev-c3c928f38ebc0ac0c6cd', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:2'}, {'id': 'ev-84af1a450301aa5252ba', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:3'}, {'id': 'ev-dbca06e364385e22f3c5', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:5'}, {'id': 'ev-345e6706309ac04ee927', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'locator': 'page:36'}, {'id': 'ev-98a30db9253fff6cc9da', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'loca