, 'required': True, 'page': 45, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4456, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-75546d247dedb90561b5', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:46', 'required': True, 'page': 46, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4646, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:47', 'required': True, 'page': 47, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 5018, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-aa9b9dbdfec8c640b495', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:48', 'required': True, 'page': 48, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4375, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-6e64db9ec6bfa8f9417f', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:49', 'required': True, 'page': 49, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4295, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-42cada09d7411017eb46', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:50', 'required': True, 'page': 50, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4663, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:51', 'required': True, 'page': 51, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 3844, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:52', 'required': True, 'page': 52, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4072, 'exposed': True}], 'notes': {'overview': {'id': 'overview', 'content': 'Pages 1-3: Paper defines agentic LLMs as LLMs that (1) reason, (2) act, (3) interact; literature is organized according to these three categories. Contributions list adds details: category 1 = reasoning, reflection, retrieval to improve decision making; category 2 = tools and robot integration producing assistants in medicine/finance; category 3 = interaction, multi-agent simulations, role-playing, open-ended agent societies, emergent behavior. Figure 1 gives a virtuous cycle: retrieval enables tool use, reflection improves multi-agent collaboration, reasoning benefits all; feedback loops generate new training data. A research agenda is in Section 5, Table 4. Still to read: Section 1.2 Literature Selection (p.5) for search methods, Section 2 (reasoning, p.8-19), Section 3 (acting, p.20-30), Section 4 (interacting, p.31-47), Section 5 (p.48-52).', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-03c9580cc4ea3469a3d3', 'ev-84af1a450301aa5252ba', 'ev-c3c928f38ebc0ac0c6cd'], 'valid': True, 'request': 3}, 'tool_use': {'id': 'tool_use', 'content': 'Tool use (pages 20-23): agents act through APIs, robotic planning and vision-language-action models. Toolformer self-trains to decide which API to call, when, which arguments, and how to use results; it tests a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar. ToolBench contains 16,464 RapidAPI APIs; ToolAlpaca covers 400 APIs and 3938 instances; Gorilla adds APIBench. Shen et al. split planner, caller and summarizer across different LLMs. Tool selection and result summarization remain difficult skills.', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62', 'ev-7f4d5e2fe0886c80c09b', 'ev-e5b9499e130a976eefe2'], 'valid': True, 'request': 13}}, 'answers': {'reasoning': {'self_consistency_selection': {'answer': 'majority voting', 'evidence_id': 'ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3', 'page': 10, 'quote': 'Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.'}, 'tot_search': {'answer': ['breadth_first', 'depth_first'], 'evidence_id': 'ev-4049593a30e2846f8394', 'page': 13, 'quote': 'The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.'}}, 'tool_use': {'toolformer_tools': {'answer': ['calculator', 'question_answering', 'search_engine', 'translation', 'calendar'], 'evidence_id': 'ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62', 'page': 23, 'quote': 'A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar.'}, 'toolbench_api_count': {'answer': 16464, 'evidence_id': 'ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62', 'page': 23, 'quote': 'ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI, a large dataset of publicly available REST APIs.'}}, 'outlook': {'agenda_topics': {'answer': ['training_data', 'hallucination', 'agent_behavior', 'self_reflection', 'safety'], 'evidence_id': 'ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9', 'page': 51, 'quote': '         Topic               Challenge\\n         Training Data       Finetune with inference time reasoning data\\n                             Convergent/stable reinforcement learning\\n                             VLA, Multimodal signals, such as speech\\n         Hallucination       Use Self Verification\\n                             Use Mechanistic Interpretability\\n                             Use Open Ended/Open World Models for exploration\\n         Agent Behavior      Scalable simulation infrastructure, role playing\\n                             Distill reasoning to small models\\n                             Models of agent and human behavior, emergent behavior, future of society\\n         Self reflection     In-model self reflection and metareasoning\\n                             Metacognition, personality\\n                             Automated Scientific Discovery\\n         Safety              Assistants: Responsibility, liability\\n                             Privacy, fairness of data\\n                             Wider application areas for assistants\\n                                Table 4. Summary of Research Agenda for Agentic LLM'}, 'shared_foundations': {'answer': ['reasoning', 'self_verification'], 'evidence_id': 'ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3', 'page': 52, 'quote': 'Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.'}}, 'multi_agent': {'camel_prompting': {'answer': 'inception_prompting', 'evidence_id': 'ev-98a30db9253fff6cc9da', 'page': 37, 'quote': 'By using inception prompting and role descriptions, the agents stay in character and collaborate toward the goal by breaking down complex problems in manageable steps through dialogue.'}}, 'overview': {'search_methods': {'answer': ['google_scholar', 'snowballing'], 'evidence_id': 'ev-dbca06e364385e22f3c5', 'page': 5, 'quote': 'The papers were initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach to discover work that was cited but not yet included in our initial set.'}}}, 'section_text': {}}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone", "observations_images": null, "action_output": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 8411, "output_tokens": 753, "total_tokens": 9164}, "is_final_answer": false}}
